{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id1698618174"}, "name":{"label":"Корзаков"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-10-18T21:52:43-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.2026.279"}, "id":{"label":"14684209157"}, "title":{"label":"One ai assistant"}, "content":{"label":"I would like to express my sincere appreciation to the OpenAI team for creating ChatGPT, for its intuitive interface, seamless user experience, and the extraordinary possibilities your application makes available to people around the world.\n\nWe are living in a truly remarkable era, in which artificial intelligence is becoming a powerful tool for human development, expanding our capabilities and potentially opening a new chapter in the evolution of humanity. Thank you, OpenAI, for your contribution to this transformation! I hope ChatGPT will continue to evolve, becoming even more capable, accessible, and convenient for people everywhere.\n\nI have one important feature request.\n\nI would love to use a single AI assistant — ChatGPT — as my primary companion for work, learning, planning, and managing my daily life. Unfortunately, the current limitations of MCP integrations in the ChatGPT mobile app make this difficult, forcing me to rely on other AI services for certain tasks.\n\nFor example, Claude allows me to connect external services on my mobile device, including Apple Reminders and Calendar. This is incredibly convenient: AI becomes more than a conversational partner — it becomes a practical assistant that can interact with my personal productivity system. Having access to these integrations, even on a free plan, is especially valuable.\n\nI would love to see similar capabilities in ChatGPT. I want to manage my tasks, reminders, calendar, and other connected tools directly through ChatGPT, without switching between AI services or manually copying commands from one application to another.\n\nMy requests to the OpenAI team are:\n\n* Add MCP integration support to the ChatGPT mobile app.\n* Enable connections to services such as Apple Reminders, Apple Calendar, and other tools for managing everyday life.\n* Make these capabilities available on all subscription plans, including the Free plan, at least with a basic level of functionality.\n\nI believe the future of AI lies not only in the quality of its responses but also in its ability to integrate seamlessly into people’s lives, help them take action, and free up their attention for what truly matters.\n\nThank you for everything you have already created. I hope ChatGPT will continue to evolve into an open and extensible ecosystem where people can choose a single primary AI assistant to help them manage the majority of their everyday tasks.\n\nI look forward to seeing these capabilities in future updates!", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=6448311069&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
